Project Tahoe — live session (Hyprland + MacShell).

The desktop starts automatically on tty1. For a plain shell press
Ctrl+Alt+F2 … F6 and log in as `root` (no password on the live image)
or as `tahoe`.

Keybinds:
  SUPER+Space   Spotlight            SUPER+Return  terminal (kitty)
  SUPER+V       clipboard history    SUPER+Q       close window
  SUPER+period  emoji picker         SUPER+F       float/un-float
  Alt+Tab       app switcher         SUPER+M       maximize
  Print         screenshot           SUPER+C       center window
  Ctrl+Alt+W    wallpaper picker     SUPER+1..5    workspaces
  SUPER+L       lock screen          SUPER+SHIFT+R reload config

`sudo` works without a password while you are on the live image.

Preinstalled from the Tahoe project: `tahoe-uel` (probe a .exe/.app/.dmg and
see the honest run plan it would choose) and `tahoe-compositor`. Try:

    tahoe-uel probe /usr/bin/kitty

The desktop is MacShell, vendored from https://github.com/0-ss/MacShell (MIT).
